ibrary owner per [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]process, and check-run triage attaches the owning task bead. The [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]lander then continues the backlog chain with the next five beads.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202611/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]backlog_epic_cmdsub_retries_launches.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202611/backlog_epic_cmdsub_retries_launches.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-1tc[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-1tc/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Model output never reaches host $(cmd) (sase-1sn)[/bold #D7AFFF]             [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]cmdsub[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cmdsub: close every model-output and agent-writable channel into host [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]command substitution for human-launched workflows, keeping macro [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]expansion and Jinja semantics.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Provider retry never re-runs an agent for a host finalizer [/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]failure (sase-1he)[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]retry_scope[dim] · [dim][/dim]after cmdsub[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]retry_scope: type host finalizer and publish failures so provider retry [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]patterns never match them, while real provider 500s still retry.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]A scheduler stop never silently drops a chop's launch batch [/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n      [bold #D7AFFF](sase-1c2)[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]chop_launch[dim] · [dim][/dim]after retry_scope[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]chop_launch: journal in-flight chop launch batches and resume them [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]idempotently after a scheduler or service-host stop, with visible [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]notices.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]beads.db has one SQLite library owner per process (sase-1kp)[/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]beads_db_owner[dim] · [dim][/dim]after chop_launch[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]beads_db_owner: remove the Rust lock-file and Python WAL-mirror [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]collision on beads.db per the mirror_fix decision, with a same-process [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]repro test.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Failure triage attaches the owning task bead (sase-1ha)[/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]triage_owners[dim] · [dim][/dim]after beads_db_owner[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]triage_owners: root-cause and fix empty possible_owners in check-run [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]triage so exact node and location matches attach the open task bead.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","created_epic_ids":["sase-1tc.1.1"],"epic_bead_id":"sase-1tc","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-6-astra","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-1tc.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","role_suffix":"plan","vcs_provider":"GitHub","workflow_name":"sase-1tc.1"},"source_run_id":"run-d3ff021c68dec79e4f9f6dec16e740b9","started_at":"2026-11-17T16:21:51.000226+00:00","state":"active"},{"capabilities":{"durably_revivable":true,"historically_viewable":true,"missing_requirements":[],"restartable":true},"commits":[],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"commits":{"digest":"12e9b8184a7b348a090fe45058aedebfb22cf1da50e50fb24211a7f15addd521","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-1tc.2/commits.js